<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zuiderzee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zuiderzee was a shallow inlet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> in the north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, enlarged by storm floods in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Ports such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampen">Kampen</a>, Harderwijk, Enkhuizen and Hoorn traded across it. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsluitdijk">Afsluitdijk</a> closed it off in 1932, turning it into the freshwater IJsselmeer, and large parts were then drained to create new polders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zuiderzee.jpg" alt="Zuiderzee" width="320" height="276" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Janssonius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seven_United_Netherlands_Janssonius_1658.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
